  "flavor": {
    "name_bank_key": "gormdurn",
    "phonemic_palette": "Gormdurn (Durnkad fire-dialect): the shared hard-frame/soft-vowel/short-syllable Durnkad, with the fire-dialect drift - word-final and medial stops GEMINATE (-un -> -unn, -ak -> -akk), o raises toward u, and the whole has a crackling, clipped, anvil-loud edge. The common-word stock is the shared Durnkad (one tongue); the gemination shows in speech and in the marked forms (titles, deities, the realm's own name).",
